From 9d9df81ec47e02968ff1233d1722024f7f33c282 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mechatronics-studio
 <67246298+mechatronics-studio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:40:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(model): a linked model's digest is of the bytes the
 import parsed

ImportModel::within read the file, parsed it, then read it again for the
link's SHA-256: a file that changed between the two reads recorded the
newer digest over the older mesh, and the change was never imported.
The import now reads once (geometry/import/sourced.rs): a buffered
format hashes the buffer it parses, and STL is hashed as its streaming
parse reads it. The kernel SHA-256 takes bytes in pieces, and the link
check hashes a file in 1 MiB pieces instead of reading it whole.

Fixes #2689

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
